%C - SMBus Byte/Word Utility.
Execute DCMD_SMBUS_CMD devctl with the following commands:
    - SMBUS_CMD_BYTE (1-byte payload)
    - SMBUS_CMD_BYTE_DATA (2-byte payload)
    - SMBUS_CMD_WORD_DATA (3-byte payload)


Usage:

%C -a address [-l length] [-n bus_path] [-v[v...]] [--pec] [--raw] [data]...


Options:

-a address, --addr=address
    Set the 7-bit slave address

-l length, --len=length
    Set the number of bytes to receive
    (default: 0)

-n bus_path, --path=bus_path
    Specify the location of the SMBus resource manger to attach to
    (default: /dev/smb0)

-v[v[v...]], --verbose=<level>
    Set the verbosity level of displayed details
    (default: 0)

--pec
    Enable the Packet Error Code (PEC) feature
    (default: disabled)

--raw
    Display the received bytes as unformatted output
    (default: disabled)

data
    Specify the bytes to send


Examples:

- Read one byte of device 0x73 (SMBUS_CMD_BYTE)
%C -a 0x73 -l 1

- Write the byte 0xAA in device 0x73 (SMBUS_CMD_BYTE)
%C -a 0x73 0xAA

- Read one byte at offset 0x02 of device 0x50 (SMBUS_CMD_BYTE_DATA)
%C -a 0x50 -l 1 0x02

- Write the byte 0xAA at offset 0x02 in device 0x44 (SMBUS_CMD_BYTE_DATA)
%C -a 0x44 0x02 0xAA

- Read two bytes at offset 0x02 of device 0x50 (SMBUS_CMD_WORD_DATA)
%C -a 0x50 -l 2 0x02

- Write the word 0xBBAA at offset 0x02 in device 0x44 (SMBUS_CMD_WORD_DATA)
%C -a 0x44 0x02 0xAA 0xBB
